WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:17.497
Ethan looked at his permission slip.

2
00:00:17.498 --> 00:00:22.489
The campers were going to Sunnydale Park today, but he didn't know why.

3
00:00:22.490 --> 00:00:25.699
Then Mr. Dunn solved the mystery.

4
00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:28.968
"The Kite Festival is at the park today.

5
00:00:28.969 --> 00:00:34.009
And we're going to participate!"

6
00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:37.390
"But we don't have kites," said Jason.

7
00:00:37.391 --> 00:00:42.365
"Not yet. But we will soon," Mr. Dunn said.

8
00:00:42.366 --> 00:00:46.409
"Are we going shopping for kites?" Izzie asked.

9
00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:53.690
Mr. Dunn laughed. "We're going to make our kites, Izzie."

10
00:00:53.691 --> 00:00:56.936
Izzie cheered, but Nina frowned.

11
00:00:56.937 --> 00:01:00.199
"That sounds hard," she said.

12
00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:02.959
"It's actually very easy."

13
00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:06.543
Mr. Dunn pointed to the table.

14
00:01:06.544 --> 00:01:12.232
"If we attach strings and tails to these paper bags, they should fly."

15
00:01:12.233 --> 00:01:17.255
"That sounds fun," said Ethan. "Let's get started."

16
00:01:17.256 --> 00:01:23.940
"First find the top of your bag, where it opens," said Mr. Dunn.

17
00:01:23.941 --> 00:01:29.677
"With masking tape, mark the four corners, two on each side.

18
00:01:29.678 --> 00:01:33.618
After that we'll punch a hole in each corner."

19
00:01:33.619 --> 00:01:37.550
The kids marked the corners.

20
00:01:37.551 --> 00:01:42.025
Then they punched the holes.

21
00:01:42.026 --> 00:01:47.653
"Now we need to add string to fly our kites," said Mr. Dunn.

22
00:01:47.654 --> 00:01:55.152
"Cut two pieces of string 75 centimeters long.

23
00:01:55.153 --> 00:01:59.666
Thread one string through the left hole on one side of the bag.

24
00:01:59.667 --> 00:02:03.648
Tie a knot so the string won't slip through.

25
00:02:03.649 --> 00:02:10.657
Then thread the other end of the string through the right hole and knot it," said Mr. Dunn.

26
00:02:10.658 --> 00:02:17.164
"Repeat on the other side."

27
00:02:17.165 --> 00:02:21.598
"Hey!" said Izzie. "I made two loops!"

28
00:02:21.599 --> 00:02:25.725
Next Mr. Dunn told them how to make the handles.

29
00:02:25.726 --> 00:02:31.700
"Cut a string 100 centimeters long.

30
00:02:31.701 --> 00:02:36.435
Pull it through the two loops you just made," Mr. Dunn continued.

31
00:02:36.436 --> 00:02:38.983
"And tie the ends."

32
00:02:38.984 --> 00:02:42.364
Mr. Dunn checked everyone's handles.

33
00:02:42.365 --> 00:02:47.237
"Fantastic! Now we're ready to decorate."

34
00:02:47.238 --> 00:02:52.141
"There will be lots of kites at the festival," said Mr. Dunn.

35
00:02:52.142 --> 00:02:57.153
"So paint your name in huge letters on your kite.

36
00:02:57.154 --> 00:03:03.509
After that, cut up some streamers and glue them to the bottom of your bag.

37
00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:07.495
Any questions?" Mr. Dunn looked around.

38
00:03:07.496 --> 00:03:11.670
"Nope." Ethan had already started painting.

39
00:03:11.671 --> 00:03:16.923
"I like those polka dots," said Izzie. "Very colorful!"

40
00:03:16.924 --> 00:03:22.651
"Thanks," said Ethan, adding orange and yellow streamers to the bottom of the bag.

41
00:03:22.652 --> 00:03:26.694
"I want my kite to look like a flaming comet!"

42
00:03:26.695 --> 00:03:30.707
After lunch it was finally time to go to the festival.

43
00:03:30.708 --> 00:03:35.173
"This looks really cool," Ethan said, admiring his kite.

44
00:03:35.174 --> 00:03:40.372
He tucked it under his arm and lined up behind Mr. Dunn.

45
00:03:40.373 --> 00:03:43.914
Ethan couldn't believe how crowded the park was.

46
00:03:43.915 --> 00:03:47.715
He didn't know there were so many kite-lovers in Sunnydale!

47
00:03:47.716 --> 00:03:51.322
Mr. Dunn pointed to an empty patch of grass.

48
00:03:51.323 --> 00:03:57.984
"We can launch our kites over there," he said.

49
00:03:57.985 --> 00:03:59.910
Ethan looked up.

50
00:03:59.911 --> 00:04:06.204
The sky was colorful as kites flew in every direction.

51
00:04:06.205 --> 00:04:11.724
"I'm worried," Jason said. "Maybe our kites won't fly."

52
00:04:11.725 --> 00:04:15.098
"You won't know until you try," Ethan said.

53
00:04:15.099 --> 00:04:20.145
"Come on!" He grabbed his kite's handle and started to run.

54
00:04:20.146 --> 00:04:25.679
"Yeah! Let's go!" Izzie grabbed her kite and ran after Ethan.

55
00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:29.160
Both of their kites took off in the wind.

56
00:04:29.161 --> 00:04:32.802
Ethan weaved through the crowd with his kite soaring.

57
00:04:32.803 --> 00:04:36.994
Everyone's kites were different, but they all looked great.

58
00:04:36.995 --> 00:04:39.996
Soon he saw Jason following him.

59
00:04:39.997 --> 00:04:42.790
Jason's kite was in the air too.

60
00:04:42.791 --> 00:04:54.190
"Doesn't it feel good to fly?" Ethan shouted.
